Cell["\<\
The three numbers are three readings of the same five events. Classical: \
assign each event a definite 0 or 1 in advance; exclusivity forbids two \
adjacent 1s, so at most two events fire \[LongDash] \[Alpha](C5) = 2. \
Quantum: assign each event the probability cos^2 of an actual measurement \
direction against an actual state; the pentagon geometry below lets every \
event carry 1/\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] 0.447 simultaneously \[LongDash] summing \
to \[CurlyTheta](C5) = \[Sqrt]5. Exclusivity-only: forget mechanics entirely \
and demand only that adjacent events never both fire; probability 1/2 \
everywhere is then legal \[LongDash] \[Alpha]*(C5) = 5/2. One pentagon, three \
ceilings:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e9942a67-109c-ba49-9c9f-e495b4c5ca9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\[FilledRightTriangle] ",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.55]],
 StyleBox["Born rule (measurement postulate)",
  FontSize->11,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3]],
 StyleBox["  \[Bullet] |\:3008handle|v_k\:3009|\.b2, cos\.b2 click \
probability, probability = |amplitude|\.b2, expectation \:3008\[Psi]|A|\[Psi]\
\:3009, 'Mean' as expectation value",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.45]]
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 CellMargins->{{86, 30}, {1, 
  5}},ExpressionUUID->"8834b376-c26c-6949-b0db-982e3b917b09"],

Cell["\<\
The postulate fixing how quantum states yield statistics: measuring an \
observable with projectors {P_k} on state |\[Psi]\:27e9 gives outcome k with \
probability p(k) = \:27e8\[Psi]|P_k|\[Psi]\:27e9; for a rank-one projector \
P_k = |v_k\:27e9\:27e8v_k| this is the squared overlap \
|\:27e8v_k|\[Psi]\:27e9|\.b2, and the expectation value of any observable A \
is \:27e8A\:27e9 = \:27e8\[Psi]|A|\[Psi]\:27e9. After outcome k, the state \
updates to P_k|\[Psi]\:27e9/\[Sqrt]p(k). Every probability in this essay is a \
Born-rule value \[LongDash] each KCBS projector clicks on the handle state \
with |\:27e8handle|v_k\:27e9|\.b2 = 1/\[Sqrt]5, QuantumMeasurementOperator's \
\"Mean\" returns \:27e8\[Psi]|P|\[Psi]\:27e9, and the 25 composite projectors \
P_i \[CircleTimes] P_j click with probability exactly 1/5.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{104, 30}, {4, 4}},
 FontSize->12,ExpressionUUID->"151669d2-ac35-d444-9865-91615c5499c7"],

Cell["\<\
Read the same pentagon three ways \[LongDash] best classical assignment, \
quantum weights, bare-exclusivity halves:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"2e2871c6-7433-ba4e-b6fa-4983abab11c5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Module[{pts, pent, blue, amber}, blue = RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85]; amber = \
RGBColor[0.85, 0.55, 0.2]; pts = Table[{Cos[Pi/2 + 2*Pi*(q/5)], Sin[Pi/2 + \
2*Pi*(q/5)]}, {q, 0, 4}]; pent = Function[{vals, cols, sVal, title, sub}, \
Labeled[Graphics[{{GrayLevel[0.65], Thickness[0.006], Line[Append[pts, \
First[pts]]]}, Table[{cols[[q]], EdgeForm[GrayLevel[0.35]], Disk[pts[[q]], \
0.2], If[MatchQ[cols[[q]], GrayLevel[_]], Black, White], \
Text[Style[vals[[q]], 10, Bold], pts[[q]]]}, {q, 1, 5}]}, ImageSize -> 190, \
PlotRange -> 1.45, PlotRangePadding -> 0.12], Column[{Style[title, Bold, 10], \
Style[sub, Italic, 8, GrayLevel[0.45]], Style[StringJoin[\"\[CapitalSigma]p = \
\", sVal], 13, Bold]}, Alignment -> Center, Spacings -> 0.25], Top]]; \
Row[{pent[{\"1\", \"0\", \"1\", \"0\", \"0\"}, {blue, GrayLevel[0.82], blue, \
GrayLevel[0.82], GrayLevel[0.82]}, \"2\", \"CLASSICAL\", \"best 0/1 \
assignment: \[Alpha](C5)\"], pent[{\".45\", \".45\", \".45\", \".45\", \
\".45\"}, ConstantArray[blue, 5], \"\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeEqual] 2.236\", \"QUANTUM\
\", \"cos^2 weights: \[CurlyTheta](C5)\"], pent[{\"1/2\", \"1/2\", \"1/2\", \
\"1/2\", \"1/2\"}, ConstantArray[amber, 5], \"5/2\", \"EXCLUSIVITY ONLY\", \
\"no-signalling ceiling: \[Alpha]*(C5)\"]}, Spacer[8]]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,ExpressionUUID->"76ad9908-5616-ed4e-be19-a5c09c185ef1"],

