Cell["\<\
KCBS takes its name from Klyachko, Can, Binicioglu and Shumovsky (2008), who \
derived what they called the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]pentagram inequality\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] for a three-dimensional quantum system (a qutrit): \
five unit vectors on a cone, each orthogonal to its two cyclic neighbors, \
giving five dichotomic observables A_i = 1 - 2|v_i\[RightAngleBracket]\
\[LeftAngleBracket]v_i| with eigenvalues \[PlusMinus]1. Because neighboring \
directions are orthogonal, the pair (A_i, A_i+1) is jointly measurable \
\[LongDash] exactly the five edges of the C5 exclusivity graph above. Any \
noncontextual hidden-variable assignment obeys the cyclic sum \[CapitalSigma] \
\[LeftAngleBracket]A_i A_i+1\[RightAngleBracket] \[GreaterEqual] -3; the \
qutrit instead reaches \[CapitalSigma] = 5 - 4\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] -3.944 \
at the cone-axis state, where each projector has quantum probability \
1/\[Sqrt]5.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a370bb3-7599-a14b-9c7b-26538e9b7826"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\[FilledRightTriangle] ",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.55]],
 StyleBox["KCBS inequality",
  FontSize->11,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3]],
 StyleBox["  \[Bullet] pentagram inequality, \[CapitalSigma]\:3008A_i A_(i+1)\
\:3009 \[GreaterEqual] \[Minus]3, quantum value 5\[Minus]4\[Sqrt]5, Klyachko\
\[Dash]Can\[Dash]Binicio\:011flu\[Dash]Shumovsky (2008)",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.45]]
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 CellMargins->{{86, 30}, {1, 
  5}},ExpressionUUID->"3f42d1d5-a615-804f-8cd8-335b8a708dad"],

Cell["\<\
The KCBS inequality (Klyachko, Can, Binicio\:011flu, Shumovsky, 2008), \
originally the \"pentagram inequality\", is the minimal test of quantum \
contextuality. Five unit vectors v_0\[Ellipsis]v_4 in a qutrit's state space, \
each orthogonal to its two cyclic neighbors, define dichotomic observables \
A_i = 1 \[Minus] 2|v_i\:27e9\:27e8v_i|; adjacent pairs commute and are \
jointly measurable \[LongDash] the edges of the pentagon exclusivity graph \
C5. Every noncontextual assignment of preexisting \[PlusMinus]1 values obeys \
\[CapitalSigma]\:27e8A_i A_(i+1)\:27e9 \[GreaterEqual] \[Minus]3 (indices mod \
5), whereas the qutrit's cone-axis state gives each context \:27e8A_i A_(i+1)\
\:27e9 = 1 \[Minus] 4/\[Sqrt]5, summing to 5 \[Minus] 4\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] \
\[Minus]3.944. On the event ruler, \[CapitalSigma]\:27e8A_i A_(i+1)\:27e9 = 5 \
\[Minus] 4\[CapitalSigma]p, so the bounds read \[CapitalSigma]p \[LessEqual] \
2 versus \[Sqrt]5 = \[CurlyTheta](C5).\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{104, 30}, {4, 4}},
 FontSize->12,ExpressionUUID->"e661c86f-e7e4-c84d-ba5e-a20a2109dc08"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\[FilledRightTriangle] ",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.55]],
 StyleBox["projector (projection operator)",
  FontSize->11,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3]],
 StyleBox["  \[Bullet] |v_k\:3009\:3008v_k|, Outer[Times,v,v], rank-1 \
projection, tensor-product projectors P_i \[CircleTimes] P_j",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.45]]
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 CellMargins->{{86, 30}, {1, 
  5}},ExpressionUUID->"44b9842d-17d4-a54a-9cbb-b92093a5e35c"],

Cell["\<\
A projector is a Hermitian, idempotent operator: P\[Dagger] = P and P\.b2 = \
P. The essay uses rank-1 projectors P_k = |v_k\:27e9\:27e8v_k| (in code, \
Outer[Times, v, v]), each projecting onto the ray spanned by a unit vector \
v_k. Measuring P_k is a yes/no test: on state |\[Psi]\:27e9 it \"clicks\" \
with probability \:27e8\[Psi]|P_k|\[Psi]\:27e9 = \
|\:27e8v_k|\[Psi]\:27e9|\.b2, its eigenvalues being 1 (yes) and 0 (no). \
Orthogonal directions give commuting projectors with P_i P_j = 0, i.e. \
mutually exclusive events \[LongDash] the pentagon's edges. Every object here \
is built from projectors: the dichotomic observables A_k = 1 \[Minus] 2|v_k\
\:27e9\:27e8v_k|, and the 25 joint tests P_i \[CircleTimes] P_j on two \
independent pentagon copies.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{104, 30}, {4, 4}},
 FontSize->12,ExpressionUUID->"8f9be8ac-3c5c-bb4e-a071-73f50bf2efd7"],

Cell["\<\
Verify the cone-angle geometry live: the per-event quantum probability, and \
that summing it over all five pentagon events reproduces \[CurlyTheta](C5):\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"d21b02c5-cf68-9c4a-9e42-8c7c90b2126c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Simplify[{Cos[Pi/5]/(1 + Cos[Pi/5]), 5*Cos[Pi/5]/(1 + Cos[Pi/5])}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,ExpressionUUID->"1a374cc0-b825-0c42-91dd-cf666024adc2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", 
    SqrtBox["5"]], ",", 
   SqrtBox["5"]}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b88a96f2-6b32-4445-83bd-\
e0bf43974c26"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The geometry deserves to be seen, and its numbers deserve operational \
meaning. Each direction v_k is a detector; on the handle state (the cone's \
axis) it clicks with probability |\[LeftAngleBracket]handle|v_k\
\[RightAngleBracket]|^2, and since all five rays lean on the axis at the same \
angle, all five click probabilities are equal \[LongDash] the blue curve. \
Exclusivity is the second, sharper requirement: adjacent directions must be \
perpendicular, so that their projectors commute and can be tested in a single \
run \[LongDash] and if v_k has just fired, the probability that its neighbor \
v_(k+1) also fires is the squared overlap |\[LeftAngleBracket]v_k|v_(k+1)\
\[RightAngleBracket]|^2, which must be EXACTLY zero for the two events to be \
mutually exclusive. That crosstalk between supposedly-exclusive detectors is \
the coral curve, and it is the quantity that makes the cone angle rigid: the \
two curves meet the KCBS specification at exactly one half-angle, \[Theta]* = \
ArcCos[5^(-1/4)] \[TildeTilde] 48.06\[Degree], where each detector clicks \
with probability 1/\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] 0.447 and the crosstalk is exactly \
zero. Five degrees of detuning already lets \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]exclusive\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] detectors co-fire 2.5% of the time. Connecting \
consecutive tips traces the pentagram that gave KCBS's inequality its \
original name; every marked value below is measured through \
QuantumMeasurementOperator, not read off the drawing:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc63dd84-438f-f642-8bcf-fb2cf38f9371"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\[FilledRightTriangle] ",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.55]],
 StyleBox["orthonormal representation with handle",
  FontSize->11,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3]],
 StyleBox["  \[Bullet] handle state, cone-axis state, vector representation, \
representation witness, rail representation",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.45]]
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 CellMargins->{{86, 30}, {1, 
  5}},ExpressionUUID->"0239ee5f-81af-eb4e-b009-3ae5a715a8c6"],

Cell["\<\
An orthonormal representation of an exclusivity graph assigns each vertex i a \
unit vector u\:1d62 so that adjacent (mutually exclusive) vertices are \
orthogonal: \:27e8u\:1d62, u\:2c7c\:27e9 = 0 whenever i ~ j \[LongDash] the \
complement of Lov\[AAcute]sz's original convention, which orthogonalizes \
non-adjacent pairs. A handle (Gr\[ODoubleDot]tschel\[Dash]Lov\[AAcute]sz\
\[Dash]Schrijver's term) is one further unit vector h; the representation's \
value is \[CapitalSigma]\:1d62 \:27e8h, u\:1d62\:27e9\.b2, and the Lov\
\[AAcute]sz number \[CurlyTheta] is the maximum value over all \
representations and handles, so any explicit construction certifies a lower \
bound on \[CurlyTheta]. Each u\:1d62 defines a rank-one projector and h a \
quantum state, making \:27e8h, u\:1d62\:27e9\.b2 the click probability of \
event i; for the KCBS pentagon C5, Lov\[AAcute]sz's symmetric umbrella of \
five vectors about h gives \:27e8h, u\:1d62\:27e9\.b2 = 1/\[Sqrt]5 each, \
attaining \[CapitalSigma]p = \[Sqrt]5 = \[CurlyTheta](C5).\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{104, 30}, {4, 4}},
 FontSize->12,ExpressionUUID->"8ca2d531-c98e-9342-ac98-917ccf961523"],

Cell["\<\
Draw the five directions on their cone, and track both operational \
probabilities \[LongDash] per-event click rate on the handle state, and \
neighbor crosstalk after a click \[LongDash] across all cone angles, marking \
the QuantumMeasurementOperator-computed values at and near \[Theta]*:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"6216c86d-b585-a646-a4c2-556ae920176c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Module[{c2, th, vv, vecs, projsAt, handle, qClick, qCross, qCrossOff, tstar, \
blue, coral, tealc, ink, scene, curves}, blue = RGBColor[0.2, 0.45, 0.85]; \
coral = RGBColor[0.6, 0.24, 0.11]; tealc = RGBColor[0.06, 0.43, 0.34]; ink = \
GrayLevel[0.15]; c2 = Cos[Pi/5]/(1 + Cos[Pi/5]); th = ArcCos[Sqrt[c2]]; tstar \
= N[th/Degree]; vv[t_] := Table[N[{Sin[t]*Cos[4*Pi*(j/5)], \
Sin[t]*Sin[4*Pi*(j/5)], Cos[t]}, 20], {j, 0, 4}]; vecs = vv[th]; projsAt[t_] \
:= (Outer[Times, #1, #1] & ) /@ vv[t]; handle = QuantumState[{0, 0, 1}, 3]; \
qClick = QuantumMeasurementOperator[projsAt[th][[1]]][handle][\"Mean\"]; \
qCross = QuantumMeasurementOperator[projsAt[th][[2]]][QuantumState[vecs[[1]], \
3]][\"Mean\"]; qCrossOff = QuantumMeasurementOperator[projsAt[th - \
5*Degree][[2]]][QuantumState[vv[th - 5*Degree][[1]], 3]][\"Mean\"]; scene = \
Graphics3D[{{Opacity[0.12], tealc, Cone[{{0, 0, 1.02}, {0, 0, 0}}, \
1.02*Tan[th]]}, {coral, Thickness[0.006], Arrowheads[0.03], Arrow[{{0, 0, 0}, \
{0, 0, 1.24}}]}, Text[Style[\"axis = handle state\", 10, coral], {0, 0, \
1.56}], Table[{blue, Thickness[0.005], Arrowheads[0.025], Arrow[{{0, 0, 0}, \
N[vecs[[j]]]}], Text[Style[Subscript[\"v\", j - 1], 12, ink], \
1.19*N[vecs[[j]]]]}, {j, 5}], {Darker[tealc, 0.1], Thickness[0.004], \
Table[Line[{N[vecs[[j]]], N[vecs[[Mod[j, 5] + 1]]]}], {j, 5}]}}, Boxed -> \
False, ImageSize -> 300, PlotRange -> {{-1.35, 1.35}, {-1.35, 1.35}, {-0.05, \
1.68}}, ViewPoint -> {2.6, -2.2, 1.4}]; curves = Plot[{Cos[t*Degree]^2, \
(Cos[t*Degree]^2 + Sin[t*Degree]^2*Cos[4*(Pi/5)])^2}, {t, 30, 66}, PlotStyle \
-> {{blue, Thickness[0.005]}, {coral, Thickness[0.005]}}, PlotLegends -> \
Placed[{\"P(v_k clicks) on the handle state\", \"P(v_k+1 clicks) after v_k \
fired \[LongDash] crosstalk\"}, Below], FrameLabel -> {\"cone half-angle \
(degrees)\", \"probability\"}, Frame -> True, PlotRange -> {{30, 66}, {-0.04, \
0.84}}, GridLines -> {None, {0}}, GridLinesStyle -> \
Directive[GrayLevel[0.55], Dashed], LabelStyle -> Directive[10, \
GrayLevel[0.3]], ImageSize -> 370, Epilog -> {{GrayLevel[0.45], Dashed, \
Line[{{tstar, -0.04}, {tstar, 0.84}}]}, Text[Style[\"\[Theta]* = \
ArcCos[5^(-1/4)] \[TildeTilde] 48.06\[Degree]\", 10, GrayLevel[0.25]], {tstar \
+ 0.8, 0.79}, {-1, 0}], {blue, PointSize[0.02], Point[{tstar, N[qClick]}]}, \
Text[Style[\"1/\[Sqrt]5 \[TildeTilde] 0.447\", 10, blue], {tstar + 1.6, \
N[qClick] + 0.05}, {-1, 0}], {coral, PointSize[0.02], Point[{tstar, \
N[qCross]}]}, Text[Style[\"exactly 0\", 10, coral], {tstar + 1.6, N[qCross] + \
0.05}, {-1, 0}], {coral, PointSize[0.014], Point[{tstar - 5, N[qCrossOff]}]}, \
Text[Style[\"5\[Degree] off: 2.5% forbidden co-clicks\", 9, coral], {tstar - \
5, N[qCrossOff] + 0.14}, {0.25, 0}]}]; Row[{scene, curves}, Spacer[10]]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,ExpressionUUID->"9ddfcd97-2ffc-ab40-bff2-ba05a78901c5"],

