Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\[FilledRightTriangle] ",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.55]],
 StyleBox["Schur complement",
  FontSize->11,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3]],
 StyleBox["  \[Bullet] Schur-complement argument, edge-by-edge PSD assembly",
  FontSize->10,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.45]]
}], "Text",
 ShowGroupOpener->True,
 CellMargins->{{86, 30}, {1, 
  5}},ExpressionUUID->"5aa5268c-8c66-b046-bce6-8ec9a7312e9d"],

Cell["\<\
For a block matrix M = [[A, B], [B*, C]] with A invertible, the Schur \
complement of A in M is M/A = C \[Minus] B*A\:207b\.b9B. Its key property: \
when A is positive definite, M is positive semidefinite if and only if C \
\[Minus] B*A\:207b\.b9B is positive semidefinite. This turns a global \
positivity condition on a large matrix into a chain of small local checks \
\[LongDash] exactly how the essay's \[CapitalGamma]_k certificates work: one \
rational positive-semidefinite block per de Bruijn-k node is assembled \
edge-by-edge around a ring, each join justified by a Schur-complement step, \
yielding a provable per-block ceiling on the Lov\[AAcute]sz number \
\[CurlyTheta] \[LongDash] and, once the exactly-tracked classical term \
\[Alpha]/L is subtracted, on the gap density \[CurlyTheta]/L \[Minus] \
\[Alpha]/L \[LongDash] for every gluing word as seen through windows of size \
k.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{104, 30}, {4, 4}},
 FontSize->12,ExpressionUUID->"6c1bee75-9c89-234a-8e81-3b4244fc0830"],

Cell["\<\
Why ddt is special among periodic orbits: (A) the spectrum of per-block \
\[CurlyTheta]-densities of periodic gluing orbits, running from the twisted \
ring's \[Tau]* \[TildeTilde] 1.3767 up to the direct ring's 3/2, with mixed \
orbits such as 16/11, 19/13, 25/17 crowding a narrow band; (B) for each \
periodic orbit, the fixed-point value found by policy iteration plotted \
against its density \[LongDash] spurious fixed points line up on value = \
density \[Minus] 1, while the true optimum ddt alone drops to value = density \
\[Minus] 4/3, exposing the gap density 0.0698975:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"a41368e1-0bce-984b-afde-8b8c81d6adbf"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

